---
import ClassificationBadge from '../components/ClassificationBadge.astro';
import ContentSection from '../components/ContentSection.astro';
import CosmicBreathDiagram from '../components/CosmicBreathDiagram.astro';
import ContentPageLayout from '../layouts/ContentPageLayout.astro';
---

<ContentPageLayout
  metaTitle="Cosmic Breath | Cosmic Universalism"
  metaDescription="An introduction to the Cosmic Breath and its distinct structural scales."
  eyebrow="Cosmic Breath"
  title="A proposed cycle of expansion and compression"
  description="The Cosmic Breath is CU’s organizing model for a 3.108 trillion-year cycle: 2.8 trillion years of expansion followed by 308 billion years of compression."
>
  <section
    id="cosmic-breath-structure"
    class="breath-overview"
    aria-labelledby="cosmic-breath-structure-title"
  >
    <div class="breath-overview__diagram">
      <CosmicBreathDiagram />
    </div>
    <div class="breath-overview__content">
      <h2 id="cosmic-breath-structure-title">Structural scales remain distinct</h2>
      <p>
        The framework uses named tom scales as separate structural positions. In
        particular, <strong>sub-ctom</strong> is not interchangeable with
        <strong>ctom</strong>.
      </p>
      <div class="breath-overview__classification">
        <ClassificationBadge classification="cu-theoretical-proposition" />
      </div>
      <p>
        The diagram places the Observable Universe marker within ctom. This is a CU
        structural proposition, not an empirical measurement of the universe’s location.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="breath-details">
    <ContentSection id="reading-the-diagram" title="Reading the diagram">
      <ClassificationBadge slot="context" classification="cu-theoretical-proposition" />
      <p>
        The nested shells represent relationships within the CU framework. They should
        be read as a structural diagram of CU terminology, not as a scale drawing or an
        observational map.
      </p>
      <p>
        The labels sub-ztom, atom, btom, ctom, and ztom identify distinct positions in
        that structure. The central sub-ztom seed remains separate from the larger shells.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="ctom-observable-universe" title="ctom and the Observable Universe">
      <ClassificationBadge slot="context" classification="cu-theoretical-proposition" />
      <p>
        sub-ctom and ctom remain separate terms within the framework. The Observable
        Universe marker belongs within ctom and must not be interpreted as occupying
        sub-ctom.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="scope-of-the-model" title="Scope of the model">
      <ClassificationBadge slot="context" classification="cu-theoretical-proposition" />
      <p>
        The Cosmic Breath is presented as a CU model of expansion and compression across
        the framework’s full cycle. The durations stated in the page introduction are CU
        framework values; this page does not present them as established cosmological
        measurements.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>
  </div>
</ContentPageLayout>

<style>
  .breath-overview {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(16rem, 0.9fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    scroll-margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  .breath-overview__diagram { min-width: 0; }
  .breath-overview__classification { margin-top: var(--space-6); }
  .breath-details {
    display: grid;
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    gap: var(--space-12);
  }
  h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); }
  p { margin-block: var(--space-4) 0; }
  strong { color: var(--color-cyan); }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .breath-overview { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-8); }
  }
</style>
